# The shell counts what it does for a page — the page's styles resolved
# whole, the page laid out whole — and a script reads the count since a
# mark. What a reader's everyday gestures cost today is asserted here as
# it is: a hover and a wheel notch lay out nothing, and every keystroke
# into a field lays the whole page out again, which is the number the
# invalidation work brings to zero. No colour may be written as #rgb
# here: a # in a data URL starts its fragment and the rest is lost.
resize 800 500
open data:text/html,<title>Counted</title><style>body{margin:8px;font-family:"Sashfold Mono";font-size:16px;line-height:20px}.spacer{height:900px}</style><p><a href="/elsewhere">a link</a> and a field <input name="f"></p><div class="spacer">below</div>
assert-title Counted
assert-text a link
move 300 300

# Arriving styles and lays the page out once each.
mark
open data:text/html,<title>Again</title><p>once</p>
assert-title Again
assert-restyles 1
assert-relayouts 1

# A hover over a link, and off it, moves the cursor and nothing else.
back
assert-title Counted
mark
move 40 100
move 300 300
assert-restyles 0
assert-relayouts 0

# A wheel notch scrolls the page it has: no styling, no layout.
mark
wheel -1
assert-scrolled
assert-restyles 0
assert-relayouts 0

# A keystroke into a field lays the whole page out again today, once per
# key; the styles stand.
wheel 1
assert-scroll 0
focus f
mark
type abc
assert-value f abc
assert-restyles 0
assert-relayouts 3
